From: Wine Debugging Session
Subject: [PATCH] user32: Remove NtUserSetWindowFNID from DefDlgProc to fix WM_CTLCOLORDLG

When NtUserSetWindowFNID marks a dialog window at the kernel level,
WM_CTLCOLORDLG gets handled by the kernel-side handle_control_color()
in win32u/defwnd.c. The returned HBRUSH handle can get corrupted
during WoW64 handle translation, causing applications (e.g. DAL5 VN
engine) to receive an invalid value and report "SendMessage() error".

Removing the FNID assignment keeps dialog message dispatch entirely
in user mode, matching Proton's behavior and fixing the issue.

Fixes: WM_CTLCOLORDLG (0x0136) returns garbage (0x0110005e) instead
of a valid HBRUSH when sent to a dialog window under WoW64.

diff --git a/dlls/user32/defdlg.c b/dlls/user32/defdlg.c
--- a/dlls/user32/defdlg.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/defdlg.c
@@ -316,8 +316,6 @@
     DIALOGINFO *dlgInfo;
     LRESULT result;
 
-    NtUserSetWindowFNID( hwnd, MAKE_FNID(NTUSER_WNDPROC_DIALOG) );
-
     /* Perform DIALOGINFO initialization if not done */
     if(!(dlgInfo = DIALOG_get_info( hwnd, TRUE ))) return 0;
 
@@ -370,8 +368,6 @@
     DIALOGINFO *dlgInfo;
     LRESULT result;
 
-    NtUserSetWindowFNID( hwnd, MAKE_FNID(NTUSER_WNDPROC_DIALOG) );
-
     /* Perform DIALOGINFO initialization if not done */
     if(!(dlgInfo = DIALOG_get_info( hwnd, TRUE ))) return 0;
 
